=== R1. tau' with the printed pi (6.11) ===
R1  pi(g tau'(h)) - pi(g) = 2 e (d_A0 h) h^-1 e^-1                                   holds

=== R2. Repair A: tau' with pi' ===
R2a Lemma 6.1: tau'(h1 h2) = tau'(h1) tau'(h2)                                       holds
R2b Lemma 6.3: pi'(g tau'(h)) = pi'(g)                                               holds
R2c Lemma 6.5: mu(g tau'(h)) = mu(g).h                                               holds
R2d Lemma 7.2: T(g tau'(h)) = h^-1 T(g) h                                            holds

=== R3. Repair B: printed tau with mu'', T'' (w flipped in (6.18) and (7.3)) ===
R3a Lemma 6.3 (printed pi): pi(g tau(h)) = pi(g)                                     holds
R3b Lemma 6.5: mu''(g tau(h)) = mu''(g).h                                            holds
R3c Lemma 7.2: T''(g tau(h)) = h^-1 T''(g) h                                         holds
R3d T'' = delta(mu'') = first - second component                                     holds

=== R4. One formula alone does not suffice ===
R4a tau' with printed pi: Lemma 6.3 (expected false)                                 FAILS
R4b tau with printed mu: Lemma 6.5 (expected false)                                  FAILS
R4c tau with printed T: Lemma 7.2 (expected false)                                   FAILS

=== R5. The left action (6.15) induced through the projection ===
R5a repair B: pi(g1 g2) = g1 . pi(g2) with printed (6.15)                            holds
R5b repair A: pi'(g1 g2) = g1 . pi'(g2) with printed (6.15) (expected false)         FAILS
R5c repair A: pi'(g1 g2) = g1 * pi'(g2) with flipped (6.15)                          holds
R5d flipped (6.15) is a left action: (g1 g2) * gamma = g1 * (g2 * gamma)             holds

=== R6. Printed restatements of tau and mu: (6.13) and (6.22) ===
R6a (6.13) as printed, with tau (repair B)                                           holds
R6b (6.13) as printed, with tau' (repair A) (expected false)                         FAILS
R6c (6.22) as printed, (A_w, B_w) = mu(g) (repair A)                                 holds
R6d (6.22) as printed, (A_w, B_w) = mu''(g) (repair B) (expected false)              FAILS
R6e B_w = nabla0 + e^-1 (nabla0 e) under mu'' (second entry unchanged)               holds

=== R7. The infinitesimal tilted action (10.6) ===
R7a repair A (tau'): d/ds g.tau'(e^{s gamma}) = (e gamma, d_A0 gamma - [gamma, w])   holds
R7b   and = (e gamma, d_A gamma) with A = mu(g)[0] = A0 + w                          holds
R7c repair B (tau): d/ds g.tau(e^{s gamma}) = printed (10.6) (expected false)        FAILS
R7d   it is (e gamma, -d_A'' gamma) with A'' = mu''(g)[0] = A0 - w                   holds
